---
/*
 * Section 6 — it fits what you already use.
 *
 * Short section, and deliberately so. It exists to remove one objection — "another
 * system to move into" — and the fastest way to remove it is to say so and stop.
 *
 * The sub-body names Dext and Hubdoc. That is the doc's copy and it stays, but note what
 * it is doing: it says those tools are good and that we leave them alone. It claims no
 * partnership, no integration and no relationship with either, which is the line the
 * claims standard draws. Nothing here may be extended into a logo, a badge, or an
 * "integrates with" list.
 *
 * The closing line is the reversal — nothing to migrate away from — and gets its own
 * panel because it is the sentence a cautious buyer is actually looking for.
 */
---

<section class="fits">
  <div class="container fits__inner">
    <div class="fits__head">
      <h2 class="fits__title">This is not a system you have to move into.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="fits__body">
      <p class="fits__lead">
        Most practices already run eight or ten pieces of software, and the last thing any
        of them needs is an eleventh with its own login. We do not sell a platform. What we
        build works inside the tools you already have, and writes into the accounts you
        already keep.
      </p>

      <p class="fits__sub">
        That includes the good ones. If Dext or Hubdoc already handles a part of this well,
        we leave it alone and build around it. The work worth doing is almost never inside
        a tool — it is in the gaps between them. The handoffs, the re-keying, the chasing,
        and the thing one person does every Friday that has never been written down.
      </p>

      <div class="fits__closing">
        <span class="fits__closing-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M11.6 3.2 4 6.4v5.1c0 4.3 3 8.3 7.6 9.5 4.6-1.2 7.6-5.2 7.6-9.5V6.4z" />
            <path d="m8.8 11.9 2.3 2.3 4.3-4.6" />
          </svg>
        </span>
        <p>
          It also means there is nothing to migrate away from if you stop working with us.
          The records were always yours and they stay where they are.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .fits {
    background: var(--ark-cream);
    padding-block: 96px;
  }

  .fits__inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr);
    gap: 64px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .fits__title {
    font-size: var(--ark-h2);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    max-width: 16ch;
  }

  .fits__lead {
    max-width: 66ch;
    font-size: 1.16rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #4a463f;
  }

  .fits__sub {
    margin-top: 20px;
    max-width: 66ch;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #5b564e;
  }

  .fits__closing {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 18px;
    margin-top: 30px;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--ark-grey);
    border-radius: var(--ark-radius);
    padding: 26px 28px;
  }

  .fits__closing-icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    border-radius: 11px;
    background: var(--ark-green-soft);
    color: var(--ark-olive);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .fits__closing-icon svg {
    width: 22px;
    height: 22px;
  }

  .fits__closing p {
    font-size: 1.03rem;
    line-height: 1.66;
    color: var(--ark-charcoal);
  }

  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .fits__inner {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 32px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .fits {
      padding-block: 56px;
    }

    .fits__lead {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    .fits__sub {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .fits__closing {
      padding: 22px 20px;
      gap: 14px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px), (orientation: portrait) {
    .fits__title {
      text-align: center;
      margin-inline: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
